in the crypto world we hear a lot about  smart contracts but what are they and  how do they work smart contracts are  computer programs that run on the  blockchain picture a vending machine you  insert money push a button and get  something back there's no negotiation or  small talk the vending machine side of  the transaction is automated  programming responds to your inputs  smart contracts can be a bit like a  vending machine  or maybe they look like you and a friend  betting on a game or the price of ether  some smart contracts look more like  computer programs little autonomous  agents that execute a code when prompted  a lot of smart contracts run on the  ethereum blockchain which is a  distributed virtual computer  there are no keyboards or monitors just  thousands of computers running nodes of  the ethereum network your smart contract  will have all those computers verifying  that everything looks okay which takes a  little bit of time you wouldn't use this  sort of computer architecture for  anything like a self-driving car or  robot assisted surgery but this big  virtual computer does allow for  consensus there's agreement about what  happens on the network who sent money to  whom and what was executed when and  that's part of the magic check out the  crypto Story by Matt Levine for  Bloomberg businessweek  foreign
 

